Applied after virtiofs-makefile.patch. Unmounting tears the session down
through vtfs_drain, which turns off the device's virtqueue interrupts, and
upstream never turns them on again. A second mount of the share in the same
boot then has its requests answered but never completed: mount succeeds,
because it sends FUSE_INIT without waiting, and the first file operation
hangs. This patch turns the interrupts back on when a session registers its
callbacks, which every mount does. The queues are empty at that point,
because the teardown drained them.

diff --git a/sys/dev/virtio/fs/virtio_fs.c b/sys/dev/virtio/fs/virtio_fs.c
--- a/sys/dev/virtio/fs/virtio_fs.c
+++ b/sys/dev/virtio/fs/virtio_fs.c
@@ -531,6 +531,8 @@ vtfs_register_cb(struct vtfs_softc *sc, vtfs_fuse_cb forget_cb,
 			fsq->vtfsq_cb = forget_cb;
 		else
 			fsq->vtfsq_cb = regular_cb;
+		/* A previous session's vtfs_drain turned interrupts off. */
+		virtqueue_enable_intr(fsq->vtfsq_vq);
 		FSQ_UNLOCK(fsq);
 	}
 }
